00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.650
And Kamala Harris very quickly gets to the
heart of the issue, which is this is a pandemic.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:26.760
You can't just go around sacrificing whatever
or whoever you need to in order to temporarily

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.120
improve jobs numbers.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.320
Take a look at her answer on the economy.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.830
We have new job numbers out at the end of
the week, show that unemployment is at eight

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:41.310
point four percent and not great, but about
where President Obama had it in 2012.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.970
And so my question is, are you worried, despite
the fact that it's, again, not great, that

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:51.620
things are coming back to the point where
where Donald Trump could have more meat on

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.920
the bone for his economic argument that it's
coming back?

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:00.060
Listen, I want the American people to be able
to work.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:06.330
I want that we have jobs that are filled by
the hardworking people who want to work and

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.770
want to have the dignity that comes with good
work.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:16.560
But there is no question that Donald Trump
has been an abject failure and incompetent

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.850
when it comes to addressing the severe job
loss that has happened as a result of the

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.770
pandemic because he has failed to address
the pandemic itself.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:33.480
And when we look at this path, hopefully at
some point to recovery, his perspective cannot

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.850
be our perspective because his perspective
for too long is to talk about how well the

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:42.030
